<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neu-Augustusburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1660s</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Schloss Neu-Augustusburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Neu-Augustusburg is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weissenfels">Weissenfels</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, begun in 1660 for Duke Augustus of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxe-weissenfels">Saxe-Weissenfels</a> on the site of an older castle. It was the residence of the dukes of Saxe-Weissenfels until the line died out in 1746, and its chapel and court hosted a lively musical life. It now houses a museum on the town and the ducal court.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/neu-augustusburg.jpg" alt="Neu-Augustusburg" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lydia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schloss_Neu-Augustusburg_03.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
